course: dictionary
lesson: 4173
title: Goddess: a female god, and high praise
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A goddess is a female god. The word has «god» inside it, and the ending «-ess» shows it is a woman or girl. «The wise owl idea comes from ancient Greece, where the owl was the bird of Athena, the goddess of wisdom.» Athena is a woman, so goddess must mean a female god.
explain: Some words have a second, everyday meaning. «She is a goddess on the football pitch!» If you swap in «female god», the sentence makes no sense, so this is a different meaning. The words around it, football pitch, tell you that goddess here means someone greatly admired for being very good at something.
explain: Always check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. Try «The goddess of wisdom» with «the female god of wisdom»: it still works. Then try «a goddess on the pitch» with the first meaning: it fails. Good readers try more than one meaning and pick the one that fits.
fact: «Goddess» means a female god, a powerful being in some religions and myths.
fact: «Goddesses» is the plural, meaning more than one goddess.
fact: Athena was the Greek goddess of wisdom, and Freya is a goddess in Norse myths.
fact: Hindus today worship goddesses such as Lakshmi and Durga.
fact: In informal talk, «goddess» means a woman who is greatly admired, for her beauty or for being very good at something, such as «a sports goddess».
exercise: «The wise owl idea comes from ancient Greece, where the owl was the bird of Athena, the goddess of wisdom.» What is a goddess? | A river in Norway | A kind of bird | A very tall building | *A female god
exercise: Mia says about her friend, «She is a goddess at netball!» What does goddess mean here? | *Someone greatly admired for being very good at something | A bird that flies very high | A female god who lives on a mountain | A goddess statue in a museum
exercise: Find and copy the word from «Hinduism has many gods and goddesses» that means more than one goddess. | many | *goddesses | Hinduism | gods
test: Which word is the plural of goddess? | goddess's | goddessess | *goddesses | goddessies
test: «Christians, Jews and Muslims believe in one God and do not speak of goddesses.» What does this tell you? | They are the same as the Ancient Greeks | They worship many goddesses every day | *They believe in one God and do not talk about goddesses | They believe in goddesses but not in God
exam: In «She is a goddess on the football pitch», what does goddess mean? | A goddess of the woods, like Flora | *Someone greatly admired for being very good at something | A female god who lives on a mountain | A statue in a temple
